Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:14:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Input: wacom_w9000: add W9019 support

Support the W9019 protocol variant, including its split query transfer,
14-byte coordinate reports, special-packet release semantics, distance
reporting and power-off delay.

Move protocol parsing into internal helpers so each transfer length and
packet field can be checked before the driver reports input state.

The protocol facts (query command 0x2a and its 15-byte reply, the 14-byte
coordinate report and its flag bits, the soft-key marker in byte 12, the
off interval) come from the W9019 driver in drivers/input/wacom_tab/
(wacom.h, wacom_i2c.c, wacom_i2c_func.c) of Samsung's GPL-2.0 kernel for
the Galaxy Tab S3 (SM-T820).  No firmware, blob or decompiled code was
used.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
